{"id": "EUVD-2026-97683", "enisaUuid": "9625d9c9-2672-3b6b-b3aa-b4d73c0bce84", "description": "Crawl4AI before 0.9.4 contains a blind server-side request forgery vulnerability in RobotsParser.can_fetch that lets unauthenticated attackers bypass Docker server egress controls. Attackers can enable check_robots_txt and use redirects or DNS rebinding to reach internal, loopback, or cloud-metadata addresses for service discovery.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:57:08", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai/security/advisories/GHSA-f77g-77vp-r96v", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/crawl4ai-before-0.9.4-blind-ssrf-via-robotsparser-can-fetch-robots-txt-fetch"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qm8q-557r-p5w7", "CVE-2026-109239"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e10bd26c-0a14-39ea-80cd-16937c1fb1ed", "product": {"name": "Crawl4AI", "vendor": {"name": "unclecode"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.9.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "15473cf1-796b-3399-b518-93c2072dabf6", "vendor": {"name": "unclecode"}}], "isExploited": false}